{"authorityRole":"external_auditor","by":"buger","candidateKey":"","candidateKind":"","changeKey":"pr/6525","createdAt":"2026-10-03T11:32:46Z","decision":"accept_intent","decisionDigest":"sha256:65ef62b4a291a2de6c21c3eb5bec6e7aa0d4625d55202b223cc10670e31c7b95","decisionId":"rdec-fb0c0c888ad79bb8d22f959865d99340","identitySource":"github_login","packageDigest":"sha256:2a0eb80725059aa8f14c26d75edbd4c6f20be18ab54b0240ef41caf7cfeef9c8","packageIdentity":"epkg-ceaa2389618aa4f1c8c0486e2eed716ccad3c432b37761786bf4b30ca65fc20d","prNumber":"6525","reason":"Agree with the intent, with one regression to fix first: inline // comments now parse, but a whole-line comment indented with a non-ASCII space now empties the whole menu file. At head 913e112d, a trailing // comment after content parses (1 row, where quattro c05d9019 drops the file), // inside a string survives, trailing commas still parse, and menu-test.sh passes (130 ok). The regression: a no-break space, U+2028, U+3000, a vertical tab or a form feed indenting a // line, or a BOM later in the file, makes the file contribute 0 rows, because JSON.parse accepts only ASCII whitespace. Copying any such character outside a string as a plain space keeps the old behaviour. #13968 fixes the same inline-comment bug (#13493), so whichever lands second needs a rebase.","repo":"https://github.com/omacom/omarchy","schemaVersion":"reqproof.review-decision.v1","scope":"change"}
